cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below (and the accompanying paper once published)."
title: "temporal-leakage-audit: a temporal leakage-response instrument for clinical trial outcome prediction"
abstract: >-
  Software for measuring how much of a clinical-trial-outcome prediction model's reported
  skill depends on information unavailable at decision time. Implements the temporal
  leakage-response curve and leakage-attributable performance (LAP) with cluster-bootstrap
  confidence intervals, an as-of-time-censored drug-program benchmark built from Open Targets,
  ClinicalTrials.gov and PubMed, audits of the CTO and TrialBench benchmarks, a study of
  training-data memorization in LLM-based prediction, and a positivity-aware causal layer.
type: software
